10.0.0-stable.
Both are distributed under the MIT License and retain their upstream
copyrights. The release bundle includes their complete license files and the
Godot Engine third-party copyright inventory in its `licenses` directory.

    https://godotengine.org/license/
    https://github.com/godotengine/godot-cpp

Two generated files carry third-party code.

`editor/src/generated/simulation-module.ts` is the engine compiled to
WebAssembly by the pinned Emscripten SDK, and the module it embeds links parts
of the LLVM runtime that Emscripten ships (libc++, libc++abi and compiler-rt),
licensed under the Apache License 2.0 with the LLVM exception:

    https://llvm.org/LICENSE.txt

`editor/src/generated/source-v1-validator.ts` is this project's schema compiled
by Ajv, and carries Ajv's runtime helpers with it. Ajv is MIT, Copyright (c)
2015-2021 Evgeny Poberezkin:

    https://github.com/ajv-validator/ajv/blob/master/LICENSE

Nintendo 64 ROMs link libdragon. The pinned libdragon revision is released
into the public domain under the Unlicense. Its full licence is packaged by the
pinned toolchain used to build review ROMs.

    https://github.com/DragonMinded/libdragon/blob/trunk/LICENSE.md

PlayStation executables use Nugget's startup and C++ support under the MIT
License and the GNU libstdc++ runtime under GPLv3 with the GCC Runtime Library
Exception. The pinned toolchain retains the complete upstream licence texts and
release packaging copies them beside distributed console artifacts.

    https://github.com/pcsx-redux/nugget
    https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gcc-exception-3.1.html

Everything else in this repository is the project's own work, generated art and
the console font included.
